usiness with your  actions  you're talking about competition but  really this is a political motivation  it needs to stop we need to move  forwards and as i say other countries  like australia in the united kingdom and  other places around the world have  already agreed this deal it's already  gone through the regulators and they  don't see any problem with it  amazon are only arguing that the united  states for some reason does have a  problem and that that has got nothing to  do with actual monopolies or  cornering any markets it's actually  because the regulators don't like the  way amazon does business  but talking to the people at mgm i  really do get a feel that  they believe this deal is going to go  through sooner rather than later that  we're talking about weeks not months  it was a big breakthrough having this  agreement with the regulators that  they're going to shift production into  the united states  that really seem to  show that amazon want to do things a  certain way and that they want  and that maybe they understand the  problems the regulators have with the  way they do business  now i don't think that'll be a long-term  thing i think amazon knows the value of  a dollar and they'll squeeze out the  best they can the main reason why  stargate was produced in vancouver in  the first place was because of cost  production cost  so what do i think is going to happen  moving forwards  i think these meetings in the next week  are going to be really interesting i'm  hoping i'll find a few more little  tidbits to if i can share with you once  those meetings have happened  i want to get more of a feeling of what  mgm and the amazon executives really  believe is going to happen over the next  few months and then hopefully that'll  give us an idea of when we can expect  this deal to go through  i think we're bound to start hearing  more leaks and more information coming  out of amazon because they're going to  want to start shifting the public  opinion into t